00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.270
An exhilarating, thrilling chance chance
Uki-uki waku-waku chansu chansu

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.290
Eh? Freight transport?

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.560
The destination is Caine Galaxy.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.130
Does this have to do with the
Caine Galaxy Development Project?

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:40.760
That's right.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:41.030
So what are we transporting?
That's right.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.400
So what are we transporting?

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.730
A mineral prism.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.470
A mineral prism?

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:51.940
It's needed to stimulate a star in the Caine Galaxy,
by refracting external light energy towards it.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.110
Just warp it there. Mission complete.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.980
We can't. Warping it would cause
a critical flaw in the crystallographic axis.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.750
How many prisms are we transporting?

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.580
Just one.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.150
Then why so many containers?

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.160
They're decoys.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.360
Decoys?!
Decoys?!

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.560
A group of space pirates called The Devil's
Syndicate found out about this project,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:18.070
so we're sending duplicate containers on twenty
cargo ships across several different routes.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.740
So which one is the real one?

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.370
I don't know.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.300
Huh?

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.640
Does that mean we could be
transporting a decoy, too?

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.130
That's right. Also, the real container
will have a bomb planted inside.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.400
A bomb?!
A bomb?!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.850
What for?!
What for?!

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:35.940
I'm not sure. It's probably a self-destruct
mechanism just in case it gets stolen.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.220
Oh, great...
Oh, great...

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:45.180
Lots of Danger, Lots of Decoys

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.150
Of all the different routes, ours is
the most dangerous, so do you think?

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.810
Hmph. It's probably to outsmart the pirates.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.920
Which means, we're probably
carrying the prism.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.610
Why bother outsmarting them? If these pirates
are a bunch of young, good-looking hunks,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.760
I'll invite them onboard myself!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.220
There she goes again.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.130
Lame!

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.000
Yuri! What's with that music?!

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.230
Play some hard rock or something!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.740
I'm not afraid of any space pirates!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.570
Ow...

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.550
Beauty and strength
go hand in hand, don't they?

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.240
Kei, incoming alert.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.450
There have already been sixteen attacks.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.680
Patrol ships are on their way to each point.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.860
They're too late.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.430
I'm sure those ships have
been stripped naked by now.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.830
Kei, it's a preliminary report.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.760
It's got to be the Devil's Syndicate's doing.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.430
A list of the ships that were attacked, eh?

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.570
Kei?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:07.200
All right, let's prepare a nice
warm welcome for those pirates.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.300
So many ships have been attacked...

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.880
Looks like they're attacking
at random, doesn't it?

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.040
I have a hunch that they aren't.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.450
Ship approaching at three o'clock!

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:20.510
Check it out.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.660
This is merchant ship Reach from Planet Lon.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.820
Identify your ship and affiliation.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.500
Yuri, run a crosscheck.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.470
Roger.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.300
Can we get a visual?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.310
Something's definitely fishy. We just happen
to bump into a ship on this route, at this time...

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:41.710
Visual, coming up.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.230
Why you!

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.560
Identify your ship!

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.070
You just shot at us, and you're
asking for our I. D?! Hmph!

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.840
So that's your game, eh?
Then we're gonna play rough!

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:09.340
Huh?
So that's your game, eh?
Then we're gonna play rough!

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:09.600
Huh?
Look at 'em! Do you think an ordinary
merchant ship would be so heavily armed?

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.010
Look at 'em! Do you think an ordinary
merchant ship would be so heavily armed?

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.710
Keep them busy.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.810
I'm going in!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:19.470
Kei!

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.010
Honestly, she's so quick-tempered!

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.580
Respond.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.160
Respond!

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.470
Hey, respond already!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.660
Hi! So sorry to keep you waiting.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.570
Here I go!

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.480
3...

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.340
2...

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.040
1!

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:17.840
Unbelievable!

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:33.990
W-Wait!

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.090
Mughi, you fill up the elevator all by yourself.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:20.760
Mughi!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.320
Bingo! I was right.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.350
This is a Devil's Syndicate ship.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.790
Yuri, I'm linking their computer to ours.
Grab the data, will ya?

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:40.690
Got it.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:48.660
Kei, do you see this?!
They have the 3WA passcodes!

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.270
Our mission has been leaked?
Talk about sloppy work!

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.540
What's this? It says the secret code name
for the ship carrying the prism is "Sun."

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:57.630
"Sun"?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.310
But our ship is the "Lovely Angel"!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.880
The Dirty Pair?!

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.300
What?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:08.280
I see! All the ships that were attacked
had names involving the sun.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.950
That's why they were asking us
to identify our ship.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:16.290
Either way, now we know our ship is a decoy.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.060
That means they don't have
the prism yet, right?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.360
That's right. Which means
there's still work to do!

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:21.920
Kei!

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.690
Let's go, Mughi.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.850
Kei, there's a large ship approaching!

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:39.150
What?!
Kei, there's a large ship approaching!

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:39.840
What?!

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.780
I'm on my way back!

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.100
Wow, that's a tacky ship.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.490
Stand down! If you don't, you're a goner!

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:24.190
Shut up! Keep this up and you're
really going to make me mad!

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:24.730
What?!
Shut up! Keep this up and you're
really going to make me mad!

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.220
What?!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.490
Feisty as always, huh?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.160
B-Boss...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.270
Long time no see.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:37.330
Kei.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.610
H-How do you know my name?

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.840
You'll remember me soon enough.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:41.180
What's the matter, Kei?
You'll remember me soon enough.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.140
What's the matter, Kei?

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.710
Some weirdo is talking to me.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.950
How dare you insult our boss!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.440
Huh? So then...

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:50.650
...you're the captain of this pirate gang?

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:51.940
Stop!

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:54.720
Kei...

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.890
You have a friend who's a pirate?

00:09:57.890 --> 00:09:59.450
Not that I know of!

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.300
How very cold.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.830
I said I don't know you!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.990
Stop!

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.070
Let her go.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.800
That's right. It's important to be a gentleman.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.030
But Boss!

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.330
I wouldn't want to rough up
my childhood friend.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.440
Huh?

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.100
Childhood friend?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.610
W-Who are you calling
your "childhood friend"?!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.860
Maybe he's one of your delinquent
friends from back in the day?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.900
No way!

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.370
It would be impossible to
forget about me. Look closely.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.960
Ah! The annoying way you talk...

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.810
Are you... K-Kaia?!

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:48.670
I'm glad you finally remembered me.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.380
I feel sick now that I've
finally remembered you!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.370
Why?

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.350
There's at least one guy
like him everywhere you go.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:11:00.690
Just because he's a bit of a looker, he thinks
all the girls around him are in love with him!

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:03.620
Ah, I see. He does seem like the type.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:04.960
Nice to meet you.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.830
Kei, I've been looking for you.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.130
Oh, really?

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.900
Then get to the point!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.660
In short, I don't want to hurt you.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:20.110
As 3WA members, I'm sure you already know,
but we're after the mineral prism.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.280
Since we're not strangers,
why don't you help me out a bit?

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.010
Jeez, what an irritating guy.
He gives me the creeps!

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:29.550
I don't know which mission
brought you here, but...

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:32.380
...if you cooperate, I'll let you go.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.820
Let us go?

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.720
You should be begging us to let you go!

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:39.420
Do you really think you're
in any position to say that?

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:50.670
What do you want to do?

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:50.870
Ugh, he's always been nothing but trouble!
What do you want to do?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.210
Ugh, he's always been nothing but trouble!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.180
Kei, there's no need to get so upset.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.750
I just want you to tell me
the name of your ship.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.440
I believe it's called the
"Dirty Angel," or something?

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.710
Why are you asking, anyway?

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.750
There's no reason to hide it, right?

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:10.490
If you don't tell me your ship's name,
I'll be forced to attack you.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.430
So, if we tell you, you'll let us go?

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.360
You have my word, for now.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:19.200
I'd like to meet you again sometime,
under different circumstances.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.440
What a relief.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.230
Well, in that case, I'll tell you!

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.100
The name of our ship is...

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.970
...Lovely Angel of the Sun!

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.780
Boss, their name!

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.210
She leaves me no choice.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.150
Prepare to attack.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.680
Such a moron!

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.720
Attention all ships. We have found the "Sun."

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.990
We have found the "Sun."

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.600
They're on the run, headed towards
Caine Galaxy from Point 031!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.200
There's nothing I can do about it.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.570
The large ship is pursuing us from behind!

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.370
Perfect!

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:07.950
And after we just figured out
that we're a decoy.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:11.290
Might as well live up to our role
as a decoy, don't you think?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.410
That's true.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.680
Hyper acceleration!

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.330
They switched off their communicator!

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.670
Kei, turn the communicator back on!

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:32.340
Two midsize ships approaching at four o'clock!

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.740
Also, three ships at four o'clock from behind!

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.740
Awesome, just what I was hoping for!

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.840
Nanmo, check our flight path!
Let's make a dash for Caine Galaxy.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.220
That's where the Galactic Federation Army
is stationed, so once we get there,

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.650
we'll make our escape and be in the clear.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:46.420
Yeah!

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.870
Enemy ship at two o'clock!

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:03.930
I'll get past 'em!

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:10.930
Kei, hand over the container!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.280
He's still talking about that? What an idiot!

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:15.410
It's of no use to you.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.950
If we didn't need it, we would've
already given it to you!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.410
Hold down the fort, Yuri!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.120
Again, Kei?!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.860
What are you doing, Kei?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.890
If he wants it that bad, I'll give it to him!

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.060
A laser beam just blasted past us!

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:35.430
What are you doing?! You want to blow up
the container along with us, is that it?!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.430
I'm glad to hear your voice again, Kei.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.040
That makes one of us!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.220
Don't move so suddenly! Jeez!

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.580
Kei, hand over the container immediately.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:53.310
If you insist. I'll give you
something really good.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.820
A container loaded with a bomb, that is.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:07.470
So we had the real one after all?

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.770
You'll never hit us like that!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:30.790
It's set to explode if the casing
isn't removed properly, eh?

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:31.780
I see.

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:34.830
Saves me the trouble of planting a bomb.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:44.960
Sheesh, talk about overprotective casing.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:58.650
You're too slow to surround our Lovely Angel!

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.730
Kei! Kei, are you done yet?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.100
Almost! Buy me a little more time!

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.630
They're getting desperate.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.670
Kei, be a good girl and listen to me.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.230
Shut up!

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.580
What the heck? You've gotta be kidding me.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.010
I'm not kidding anyone.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.080
I'm quite serious.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:30.710
Why is it taking so long
to take down such a small ship?!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.930
What? There's still more?!

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.000
Oh, crap!

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.100
Kei, are you done yet?

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:49.370
Almost!
Kei, are you done yet?

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:50.300
Almost!

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.510
We're about to be surrounded!

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:51.770
Just a bit more!
We're about to be surrounded!

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:52.840
Just a bit more!

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:55.100
That's right. Think it over a bit more, Kei.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:56.940
That bastard.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:05.050
Kei, we can work this out amicably
if you hand over the container.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.250
I don't care for violence.

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:09.990
Prideful idiot.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.760
Or could it be that you like it rough?

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.800
Like you'll ever find out!

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.240
Kei, we can't keep running.

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:22.270
Sure we can!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.070
But we're completely outnumbered.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.970
You can't run from me.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.980
You are already my captive.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.710
Who are you calling your captive?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:35.450
Hmph! I don't know who made this,
but you've gotta do better to fool me.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.820
What's with this thing?! Jeez!

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.390
I'll say it again.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:44.120
All I want is you, and that container.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:46.820
All right, Kaia.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:50.560
I'll give you my treasure.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:10.810
Let's go.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.450
All yours, Kaia.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:16.820
Prepare the tractor beam!

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:22.260
Hurry, Yuri.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.890
Turning arm magnet off!

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:29.040
Kei, why don't you come with me?

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.400
I don't think it's a bad offer.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.310
I'm sorry, but I can't go with you.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:43.080
So think of that container
as you would me, and treasure it.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.050
You simpleton!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:46.880
Blastoff!

00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.420
Okay!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.560
All right, slide it down.

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.600
I'll make you mine someday.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.550
I think it's almost time.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.650
The container has finished loading.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.690
What is it?!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:27.160
There was a bomb in the container!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.000
What?!

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.390
Prepare to escape!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.480
We did it!

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.750
What a satisfying way to end the mission!

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:49.320
But, are you sure you wanted
to do that to your childhood friend?

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.010
A little thing like that won't kill him.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:07.030
Well, good job.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:09.070
You had me worried for a minute there, but...

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:12.840
...not only did you accomplish your mission,
you even drove away the pirates.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.380
That's some cargo you gave us.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.110
Huh?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:20.310
I bet you knew we had
the real one all along, Chief.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.950
Not at all. I just found out myself.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:27.050
You even made a bogus
keyword for them to steal.

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.420
Keyword?

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:31.080
That bogus keyword, "Sun!"

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.560
Hey, wait a minute.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.300
Have you really completed
your mission as planned?

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:39.030
Have you delivered it to the head
of the development project?

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.360
Answer me!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.140
He's getting really antsy.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.340
We can't back down now.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.810
Hey, what are you whispering to each other?

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:49.480
The container was blown
to bits along with the pirates.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:50.210
What?!

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:53.310
All those bombs came in handy, sir.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.550
How could you?!

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:57.550
O-Once again, the Dirty Pair's...

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:01.110
No, the 3WA's reputation has been disgraced!

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.720
You're getting a pay cut!

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.710
No bonus or vacation either!

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:09.960
Are you sure you want to say that?

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:12.900
That means we can do
whatever we want with it, right?

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:13.920
Yeah.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:17.890
If he's not going to recognize
our work, then so be it.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:19.610
W-What is that?

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:20.810
A switch.

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:21.910
F-For what?

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.180
It's the remote control for the microwave.

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:26.710
We removed the prism
and put it in the microwave.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:28.020
What are you going to do?!

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.650
And after all that work I did
removing it from its casing.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:31.950
Oh, well.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.320
W-Wait!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:34.590
Yes?

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:35.860
F-Fine.

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:38.290
You can take a vacation immediately!
I'll even issue a bonus!

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.060
So hurry up and deliver that mineral prism!

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:42.830
Yes, sir!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.520
Success!

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:55.540
Ah, good work.

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:04.790
He doubled our bonus and vacation!

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.890
It was an important mission.
We deserve every penny.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.580
All right, let's go have some fun!

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:49.760
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:56.240
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:02.740
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:09.410
